% ============================================================================
% simple-machine-alt-example.query.adj — a worked recall over the physics
% simple-machine-alt-example library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what's another example
% of a lever?": it states no physics fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `simple_machine_alt_example` rows and returns the alternate
% example + the table's source/locator/trust. A machine the cited spans give
% no second example for abstains honestly — the engine never invents one.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli simple-machine-alt-example.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "simple-machine-alt-example.adj"

? simple_machine_alt_example(lever, $AltEx)     % expect scissors
? simple_machine_alt_example($M, stairs)        % reverse bind — expect inclined_plane
? simple_machine_alt_example(screw, $AltEx)     % expect abstain — screw's own first-listed example ("screw") is not a distinct everyday object, and its second ("bottle caps") is already simple-machines.adj's primary row
